      "prose": "Solve $x^2 - 3x - 28 = 0$ by factorising.",
      "question": "What is the positive solution?",
      "widget": {
        "kind": "numeric",
        "answer": 7,
        "tol": {
          "abs": 0
        },
        "label": "Positive solution",
        "accept": "7",
        "wrong": [
          {
            "id": "sign",
            "value": 4,
            "tol": {
              "abs": 0
            }
          },
          {
            "id": "const",
            "value": 28,
            "tol": {
              "abs": 0
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      "feedback": {
        "correct": "$(x - 7)(x + 4) = 0$, so $x = 7$ or $x = -4$.",
        "generic": "Not quite right. Find two numbers that multiply to −28 and add to −3.",
        "byKey": {
          "sign": "You read 4 from the bracket $x + 4$. That bracket is zero at $x = -4$.",
          "const": "You used the constant as a root. Factorise first."
        }
      },
      "explain": {
        "text": "−7 and 4 multiply to −28 and add to −3. So $(x - 7)(x + 4) = 0$, giving $x = 7$ or $x = -4$."
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "r2-divide",
      "difficulty": 3,
      "skills": [
        "quad-solve"
      ],
      "prose": "Solve $4x^2 = 12x$.",
      "question": "What are all the solutions?",
      "widget": {
        "kind": "choice",
        "layout": "stack",
        "options": [
          {
            "id": "right",
            "text": "$x = 0$ or $x = 3$",
            "correct": true
          },
          {
            "id": "div",
            "text": "Only $x = 3$",
            "why": "You divided both sides by $4x$. That throws away $x = 0$."
          },
          {
            "id": "root",
            "text": "$x = \\pm\\sqrt{3}$",
            "why": "You treated it as $x^2 = 3$. The right side is $12x$, which changes with $x$."
          }
        ]
      },
      "feedback": {
        "correct": "$4x(x - 3) = 0$ gives $x = 0$ or $x = 3$.",
        "generic": "Not quite right. Move everything to one side and factorise."
      },
      "explain": {
        "text": "$4x^2 - 12x = 0$ factorises as $4x(x - 3) = 0$. So $x = 0$ or $x = 3$. Never divide by $x$ when $x$ might be 0."
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "r2-square-form",
      "difficulty": 2,
      "skills": [
        "quad-square"
      ],
      "prose": "Write $x^2 - 14x + 40 = (x - 7)^2 + q$.",
      "question": "What is $q$?",
      "widget": {
